Title: The Long Way Home
Credit: Written by
Author: GrillStudio test fixture

FADE IN:

EXT. CITY STREET - NIGHT

Rain hammers the empty street. MAYA (30s, soaked coat) walks alone under dead neon. A car HORN blares somewhere far off.

She stops at a shuttered grill house. The sign still reads OPEN.

MAYA
(to herself)
Of course it does.

INT. GRILL HOUSE - NIGHT

Embers still glow in the charcoal pit. TUNDE (60s) wipes the counter. He doesn't look up.

TUNDE
We're closed.

MAYA
The sign says open.

TUNDE
The sign is a liar. Like most things.

Maya sits anyway. Tunde sighs, and drops a skewer on the grill. It HISSES.

EXT. ROOFTOP - DAWN

Maya and Tunde watch the rain stop. Neither speaks.

CUT TO:

INT. GRILL HOUSE - DAY

Empty. Maya's coat hangs on the hook. [[Continuity: coat still wet?]]

INT. GRIL HOUSE - DAY

TUNDE (V.O.)
Some people come back.
